Controlling Claude's Output Format

When you want Claude to continue or complete a response in a specific format, you can guide it by pre-filling an assistant message with add_assistant_message().

Starting a Markdown Code Block

If you want Claude's response to begin inside a Markdown code block, pre-fill the assistant message with three backticks:

add_assistant_message(message_history, "```")

Claude will interpret this as if the assistant has already started a code block and will continue generating content inside it.

If you want to specify the language of the code block, include it after the backticks:

add_assistant_message(message_history, "```bash")

This tells Claude to continue the response as a Bash code block.

Preventing Claude from Closing the Code Block

You can use stop_sequences to stop generation when Claude attempts to close the code block:

stop_sequences=["```"]

For example:

message = client.messages.create(
    model=ANTHROPIC_MODEL,
    max_tokens=1024,
    messages=message_history,
    stop_sequences=["```"],
)

This is useful when you want to control where the Markdown block ends yourself.